{% comment %}
  Renders one UGC video tile with an optional product pill.

  Accepts:
  - video: {Object} a video setting value (Shopify Files)
  - video_url: {String} direct mp4 URL, used when no video is picked
  - poster: {Object} image setting for the poster frame
  - poster_url: {String} direct poster URL, used when no poster image is picked
  - product_item: {Object} product shown in the white pill (optional)
  - shopify_attributes: {String} block attributes for the theme editor

  Usage:
  {% render 'fuel05-ugc-tile', video: block.settings.video, video_url: block.settings.video_url, poster: block.settings.video_poster, product_item: block.settings.product, shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- if video != blank or video_url != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The card takes the tap and the keyboard, so it needs a role and a name of
    its own or a screen reader reaches a focusable thing it cannot announce.
    The video itself has no name to give, and naming it as well would read the
    card out twice, so it stays out of the tree.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Product titles go through polish-store-text like every other title on this
    store (a few are still German in the admin). Its output is escaped already.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign tile_label = 'Odtwórz wideo'
    assign pill_title = ''
    if product_item != blank
      capture pill_title
        render 'polish-store-text', text: product_item.title
      endcapture
      assign pill_title = pill_title | strip
      assign tile_label = tile_label | append: ', ' | append: pill_title
    endif
  -%}
  <div
    class="fuel05-ugc__tile swiper-slide"
    role="button"
    tabindex="0"
    aria-label="{{ tile_label }}"
    {{ shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- comment -%}
      With no poster image the first frame is the only thing that can fill the
      tile, so a clip without one asks for metadata and the browser paints that
      frame. A clip that has a poster still fetches nothing until it plays.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if video != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        One source, and the smallest one that still covers the card. A card is
        265px wide at most and every tile was serving the 1080p 7.2Mbps file,
        so a tap had to buffer a full HD stream before it could produce a
        single frame, which is what read as a dead tap.

        Two steps, because Liquid and the CDN disagree about what exists.
        video.sources holds two entries for a Files video, an m3u8 and one
        mp4, and that mp4 is the tallest transcode (measured: 606x1080 for
        every clip in this test). The loop is what picks when there is a
        choice. The rewrite is what gets the smaller file today: the CDN also
        serves the 480p and 720p transcodes, all three named off one trailing
        id, so only the rendition label in the middle of the file name
        differs, and Shopify builds its ladder downwards, so a clip with a
        1080p rendition has the 480p one. Verified 200 on all six clips this
        test ships; 5-17MB against 22-77MB. A URL carrying any other label is
        left exactly as it came.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign picked = blank
        assign tallest = blank
        for source in video.sources
          if source.format == 'mp4'
            if tallest == blank
              assign tallest = source
            elsif source.height > tallest.height
              assign tallest = source
            endif
            if source.height >= 480
              if picked == blank
                assign picked = source
              elsif source.height < picked.height
                assign picked = source
              endif
            endif
          endif
        endfor
        if picked == blank
          assign picked = tallest
        endif
        assign source_url = picked.url
        if picked.height > 480
          assign source_url = source_url | replace: 'HD-1080p-7.2Mbps', 'SD-480p-1.5Mbps'
        endif
      -%}
      <video
        class="fuel05-ugc__video"
        aria-hidden="true"
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="{% if poster != blank or video.preview_image != blank %}none{% else %}metadata{% endif %}"
        poster="{% if poster != blank %}{{ poster | image_url: width: 600 }}{% else %}{{ video.preview_image | image_url: width: 600 }}{% endif %}">
        {%- if source_url != blank -%}
          <source src="{{ source_url }}" type="video/mp4">
        {%- endif -%}
      </video>
      {%- comment -%}
        The same picture the poster attribute points at, drawn over the video as
        an image the browser cannot take away. iOS Safari drops the poster the
        moment play() is called, and preload="none" means no frame is decoded
        yet, so the card showed its own grey until the clip produced one. The
        image is frame 0 of the clip, so the swap to real frames is invisible.
        Decorative: the card above already carries the name.

        The resolution below is the poster attribute's own, so a clip with no
        poster source gets no overlay, which is the same clip that asks for
        metadata and paints its first frame itself.

        Lazy here: this grid scrolls vertically (the eager load on magyx.co
        was for horizontal swipe rows), the video's own poster attribute shows
        the same picture until the overlay arrives, and a lazy image inside a
        tile hidden on this device is never fetched.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign poster_image = poster
        if poster_image == blank
          assign poster_image = video.preview_image
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if poster_image != blank -%}
        <img
          class="fuel05-ugc__poster"
          src="{{ poster_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
          width="{{ poster_image.width }}"
          height="{{ poster_image.height }}"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          loading="lazy"
          fetchpriority="low">
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <video
        class="fuel05-ugc__video"
        aria-hidden="true"
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="{% if poster != blank or poster_url != blank %}none{% else %}metadata{% endif %}"
        {% if poster != blank %}poster="{{ poster | image_url: width: 600 }}"{% elsif poster_url != blank %}poster="{{ poster_url }}"{% endif %}>
        <source src="{{ video_url }}" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
      {%- comment -%}
        Same hold as the branch above, reading the URL the row passed instead of
        a picked video's preview image. A URL is a string and carries no size,
        so that branch states the size the rows ask the CDN for: every poster
        passed here is a frame 0 thumbnail of a 9:16 clip requested at width
        600, measured 600x1067. Nothing is laid out from it either way, because
        the overlay is sized by the card it fills, not by its own picture.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if poster != blank -%}
        <img
          class="fuel05-ugc__poster"
          src="{{ poster | image_url: width: 600 }}"
          width="{{ poster.width }}"
          height="{{ poster.height }}"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          loading="lazy"
          fetchpriority="low">
      {%- elsif poster_url != blank -%}
        <img
          class="fuel05-ugc__poster"
          src="{{ poster_url }}"
          width="600"
          height="1067"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          loading="lazy"
          fetchpriority="low">
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if product_item != blank -%}
      <a class="fuel05-ugc__pill" href="{{ product_item.url }}">
        {%- if product_item.featured_image != blank -%}
          <img
            class="fuel05-ugc__pill-thumb"
            src="{{ product_item.featured_image | image_url: width: 132 }}"
            alt="{{ pill_title }}"
            width="66"
            height="66"
            loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
        <span class="fuel05-ugc__pill-info">
          <span class="fuel05-ugc__pill-title">{{ pill_title }}</span>
          {%- comment -%}
            No "From" prefix here even though the theme's own card carries one:
            the design draws the price on a single line inside a 93px column,
            and "From 129,99 zł" needs about 124px, so the prefix wraps the pill a
            full text-line taller than drawn.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="fuel05-ugc__pill-price">{{ product_item.price | money }}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="fuel05-ugc__pill-add" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg preserveAspectRatio="none" overflow="visible" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path d="M7.53125 2.375H8.46875C8.55208 2.375 8.59375 2.41667 8.59375 2.5V13.5C8.59375 13.5833 8.55208 13.625 8.46875 13.625H7.53125C7.44792 13.625 7.40625 13.5833 7.40625 13.5V2.5C7.40625 2.41667 7.44792 2.375 7.53125 2.375Z" fill="currentColor"/>
            <path d="M3 7.40625H13.5C13.5833 7.40625 13.625 7.44792 13.625 7.53125V8.46875C13.625 8.55208 13.5833 8.59375 13.5 8.59375H2.5C2.41667 8.59375 2.375 8.55208 2.375 8.46875V7.53125C2.375 7.44792 2.41667 7.40625 2.5 7.40625H3Z" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
